<section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Find number</p>
    <h1>Find the reference number on your bill</h1>
    <p>The lookup needs the 14 digits at the top left of the bill, plus the letter printed beside them.</p>
</section>

<ol class="steps">
    <li>
        <strong>Reference number</strong>
        <span>Count 14 digits. Ignore spaces. Do not include the U or R in the number field.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>U or R</strong>
        <span>Choose the letter printed after the digits. If it is unreadable, leave U selected. R is tried automatically.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Customer ID</strong>
        <span>Some bills show a shorter customer ID above the reference number. Switch the search to Customer ID if that is the number you have.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Company name</strong>
        <span>Use the company printed on the same bill. A Multan number will not open under Lahore, and Karachi’s K-Electric number is not in this lookup.</span>
    </li>
</ol>

